# shellcheck shell=bash
# Invocation behind output/case_study/podcast_eval_summary.json,
# podcast_eval_report.csv, codex_mentis_ep05_review.json and
# codex_mentis_ep05_manifest.json: Codex Mentis episode 5 through the full
# deployed pipeline, then the structural evaluation and the check of the
# run manifest.
#
# Job 9124852 (case_study), 2026-10-18 00:09 to 00:27 BST, educ-lift, an
# NVIDIA L40S on htc-g075, from the clone
# ~/paper_speech_transcription_audit_final2 at
# code fc652ab with a clean tree, as its environment record and the run
# manifest's software block say. The record is in environment/case_study_9124852.txt beside the
# original's results on ARC. Test job 9124851 (pytest_suite, educ-lift) ran
# the whole suite from the same clone first, 2355 passed, 1 skipped,
# 1 xfailed and 1 failed, and the case study waited for it with
# --dependency=afterany. The failure was the test that compares the
# masker's count on output/case_study/ep05_raw_text.txt with the committed
# summary, which then held job 8983112's three redactions; this run's
# summary holds the four the test found. At fc652ab hpc/submit_case_study.sh
# passes transcription.py the review's two optional checks
# (--review-flag-zero-duration --review-repeated-passage-words 8
# --review-repeated-passage-window 60), which the manifest records as
# review_settings.
#
# The record's effective parameters give the 16 kHz WAV the job transcribed
# as CASE_AUDIO, since the script records the file it decoded to, and the
# recording CASE_AUDIO names below as CASE_SOURCE_AUDIO. The WAV was a
# decode an earlier run had cached beside the recording, reused because
# the stamp beside it named the recording's SHA-256. CASE_NAME is as below.
# CASE_MANIFEST was the clone's data/codex_mentis/manifest.json, which the
# script falls back to when no $DATA/codex_mentis/manifest.json exists, as
# none did on ARC. CASE_REPORT_DIR is the original noted below.
#
# The job writes the evaluation into CASE_REPORT_DIR and the transcripts,
# the review and the run manifest into the clone's output/transcripts/
# (git-ignored). The committed files are copies of those, byte for byte,
# except that git stores podcast_eval_report.csv with LF line endings where
# the job wrote CRLF.
#
# Job 8983112 (2026-10-04, educ-intract, an NVIDIA RTX A6000 on htc-g052,
# from the clone ~/paper_speech_transcription_audit_w2c at c4c7b38) is the
# run this record described before. Its results stay in
# audit2026/case_study_w2c on ARC. The RTX A6000 nodes are reserved for
# another group until October 2027, so this run used an L40S. Its text
# differs from 8983112's in eleven places, which output/case_study/README.md
# lists. Between c4c7b38 and fc652ab the code changed the masker and the
# review, not the decoding, so the differences come with the card. Job
# 8978758 (2026-10-04, code f2578b8, an RTX A6000 on htc-g050) ran the same
# job before ca75ced and c4c7b38 and failed at its structural evaluation
# (NEW-06); a copy of its transcript JSON matches 8983112's in every field
# but generated_at. The August run, job 8441879 on a Tesla P100 at 25c2582,
# wrote a text that differs from this run's in nine places. The command
# below therefore asks for the card type the original ran on, the l40s
# type.
#
# Reproduce (from the repository root on ARC), on the card type the original
# ran on. The command stops at "|| exit 1" when the recipe is missing:
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/case_study.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account=educ-lift --gres=gpu:l40s:1 hpc/submit_case_study.sh )
#
# CASE_AUDIO, CASE_NAME and CASE_MANIFEST below are the values the original
# ran with, written out so that a later change of a default, or a fetch
# manifest written under $DATA/codex_mentis, cannot change what this record
# reproduces. CASE_MANIFEST is relative to the repository root, where the
# job runs. CASE_REPORT_DIR sends a reproduction to its own directory under
# repro/, so it cannot overwrite the original in audit2026/case_study_l40s,
# and the job refuses a directory that already holds a summary unless
# OVERWRITE=1. The transcripts still go to the clone's output/transcripts/,
# over those of any earlier run with the same CASE_NAME.
# original: CASE_REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/audit2026/case_study_l40s"
CASE_AUDIO="${DATA}/codex_mentis/audio/ep05_beyond-the-cloud-reclaiming-data-sovereignty-in-speech-trans.m4a"
CASE_NAME=codex_mentis_ep05
CASE_MANIFEST=data/codex_mentis/manifest.json
CASE_REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/case_study"
